---
title: Experimentation Lifecycle
config:
    layout: elk
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> measuring: from process release (experiment released to production)

    measuring --> measurement_complete: measurement window elapses (time)
    measuring --> aborting: PO claims to abort

    aborting --> aborted: PO publishes abort reason

    measurement_complete --> analyzing: PO claims experiment for analysis

    analyzing --> measuring: PO extends experiment, resets window
    analyzing --> promoted: PO promotes experiment to feature
    analyzing --> killed: PO kills experiment
    analyzing --> iterated: PO requests experiment iteration

    promoted --> [*]: terminal (shipped) — PO files promotion chore
    killed --> [*]: terminal (abandoned) — PO files cleanup chore
    iterated --> [*]: terminal (iterated) — PO files new experiment issue
    aborted --> [*]: terminal (aborted) — PO files cleanup chore

    note right of measuring
        Resting. Experiment flag is live at its target percentage; data is accumulating. The release lifecycle has already completed for this experiment — this is post-release tracking.
        Entry: release-lifecycle transitions to released AND the issue is type:experiment.
    end note

    note right of aborting
        Working. PO claimed a live experiment to pull it. Used when the experiment is clearly misbehaving in production (hurting users, invalidating data, or blocked by an incident). Distinct from killed, which happens after analysis.
    end note

    note right of analyzing
        Working. PO reviews measurement results against the experiment's success criteria. Outcomes: extend (more data), promote (ship to all), kill (clean up, no ship), iterate (new experiment), in rare cases abort directly if new information emerges.
    end note

    note right of promoted
        Terminal (shipped). Experiment proved value; PO files a chore issue to remove the flag and make the treatment the default. Users on treatment continue to see it until the chore ships.
    end note

    note right of killed
        Terminal (abandoned). Experiment did not prove value; PO files a chore issue to remove the code path. Users revert to control.
    end note

    note right of iterated
        Terminal (iterated). Experiment produced useful signal but requires a different design. PO files a new experiment issue that enters refinement. The original issue is closed.
    end note

    note right of aborted
        Terminal (aborted). Experiment was pulled mid-flight. PO files a chore for cleanup and a postmortem-style note on what was learned.
    end note
